      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 1,
        "impression_count": 1240,
        "like_count": 9,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 2,
        "retweet_count": 1
      },
      "text": "The run:\n\n&gt; 8× RTX PRO 6000 on Higgsfield GPU Harness\n&gt; 1,340 frames at 1920×1080\n&gt; About 90 minutes, two boxes side by side\n&gt; 1,099.50 credits for the render\n\nhttps://t.co/WWpwlkcod6",
      "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2123566283568644164"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "1712267009483022336",
      "conversation_id": "2123566163732873491",
      "created_at": "2026-11-19T23:57:09.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "2123566279890186379"
      ],
      "id": "2123566279890186379",
      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 0,
        "impression_count": 171,
        "like_count": 6,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 0
      },
      "text": "The grade and the cut ran on the Mac, with no GPU time.\n\nThen have Claude write a check that fails the file on clipped highlights, black or duplicated frames, or a hard cut where a dissolve should be. You only watch a film that passed. https://t.co/bNTTcgUDUk",
      "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2123566279890186379"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "1712267009483022336",
      "conversation_id": "2123566163732873491",
      "created_at": "2026-11-19T23:56:59.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "2123566237632643132"
      ],
      "id": "2123566237632643132",
      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 0,
        "impression_count": 165,
        "like_count": 7,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 0
      },
      "text": "Fixes are fast too.\n\nShot 6 came back with a beige rose instead of a pink one. We fixed the colour and had all 140 frames back in about 10 minutes, while the other shots kept rendering. https://t.co/I2FBto5YVu",
      "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2123566237632643132"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "1712267009483022336",
      "conversation_id": "2123566163732873491",
      "created_at": "2026-11-19T23:56:56.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "2123566226224169131"
      ],
      "id": "2123566226224169131",
      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 0,
        "impression_count": 207,
        "like_count": 7,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 0
      },
      "text": "Then type /gpu in the same chat.\n\nClaude rented 2 boxes with 4 RTX PRO 6000 each, sent over the project and ran one Blender process per GPU.\n\nThe boxes started in 40–60 seconds. A 170-frame shot took 13–14 minutes on 4 GPUs. https://t.co/hR8QiMpDuQ",
      "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2123566226224169131"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "1712267009483022336",
      "conversation_id": "2123566163732873491",
      "created_at": "2026-11-19T23:56:50.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "2123566200676594119"
      ],
      "id": "2123566200676594119",
      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 1,
        "impression_count": 243,
        "like_count": 8,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 0
      },
      "text": "Lock the camera before you rent anything.\n\nClaude built the street, the light and 8 camera moves in Blender from scripts, then rendered a 640×360 preview of the whole cut on the Mac.\n\nApprove the preview, and the GPU run is the one you keep. https://t.co/FrJkM5gFz0",
      "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2123566200676594119"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "1712267009483022336",
      "conversation_id": "2123566163732873491",
      "created_at": "2026-11-19T23:56:48.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "2123566189788205430"
      ],
      "id": "2123566189788205430",
      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 0,
        "impression_count": 258,
        "like_count": 6,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 2,
        "retweet_count": 0
      },
      "text": "Have Claude measure what the eye sees.\n\nA checker script times each plant from 10% to 90% of its height. Our first growth took 32–40 frames and looked abrupt.\n\nNow large flowers take 115–124 frames to grow.",
      "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2123566189788205430"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "1712267009483022336",
      "conversation_id": "2123566163732873491",
      "created_at": "2026-11-19T23:56:47.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "2123566186214429137"
      ],
      "id": "2123566186214429137",
      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 0,
        "impression_count": 417,
        "like_count": 8,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 1,
        "retweet_count": 0
      },
      "text": "The growth starts from one sprout, spreads as a ring and then runs down the street.\n\nThe delays are scattered, so a single wide shot shows bare stone, sprouts, buds and open flowers at once. https://t.co/dGKzt2PppT",
      "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2123566186214429137"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "1712267009483022336",
      "conversation_id": "2123566163732873491",
      "created_at": "2026-11-19T23:56:44.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "2123566174780690752"
      ],
      "id": "2123566174780690752",
      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 10,
        "impression_count": 11135,
        "like_count": 203,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "reply_count": 3,
        "retweet_count": 179
      },
      "text": "The trick: don't simulate 25,800 plants frame by frame.\n\nEach species is baked once as 96 growth stages. Every planting site stores only a clock: when it sprouts and how long it takes to bloom.\n\nEach solver ran in 26–84 seconds on a Mac. https://t.co/EGQ0vIpWbd",
      "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2123566174780690752"
    },
    {
      "author_id": "1712267009483022336",
      "conversation_id": "2123566163732873491",
      "created_at": "2026-11-19T23:56:42.000Z",
      "edit_history_tweet_ids": [
        "2123566163732873491"
      ],
      "id": "2123566163732873491",
      "lang": "en",
      "public_metrics": {
        "bookmark_count": 52,
        "impression_count": 23912,
        "like_count": 286,
        "quote_count": 5,
        "reply_count": 17,
        "retweet_count": 184
      },
      "text": "25,800 flowers grow down a street in 40 seconds.\n\nClaude Fable 5.2 grew them in Houdini, then rendered the film on 8 rented GPUs in about 90 minutes.\n\nHere's the workflow, with the prompts to make your own: https://t.co/aDhzauO4xI",
      "url": "https://x.com/higgsfield_ai/status/2123566163732873491"
    },
